  "scope": "In the positive-sheet n-dimensional real hyperbolic-space model of curvature scale a>0, geodesic polar radius r gives metric dr²+(sinh(a r)/a)² dΩ² and angularly integrated radial volume element Vol(S^(n−1)) (sinh(a r)/a)^(n−1) dr.",
  "boundary": "Equations (6.2)–(6.3) and the following paragraph on printed p.644 supply the geodesic coordinate, metric and density. R=-n(n−1)a² is scalar curvature, as defined on p.638; sectional curvature is -a². The positive origin x0=1/a in the positive-sheet model supplies a>0. Positive exponential growth requires n>=2; that dimension qualification is a consequence of the formula, not an extra quoted assertion. For n=1 the density is constant and ball volume is linear. No general variable-negative-curvature comparison, packing existence, tree embedding or architectural/generalization claim is imported.",
